# evidence-volatile: \d+\.\d+s
# evidence-volatile: Installed \d+ packages? in \d+(\.\d+)?ms
# evidence-timeout: 300
#
# The real-git harness. Every test builds a throwaway repository under
# tmp_path and runs the SHIPPED scripts against it, so each name below is
# an assertion about git as it actually behaves, not about a mock.
#
# AC-015 / OT-005 are the first three: a pathspec commit records only its
# own paths, it leaves a peer's staged file staged, and the bare-commit
# contrast shows why the protocol needs the pathspec at all.
# AC-016 is the guard block. The two tests naming the index as the content
# source pin it from BOTH directions (staged-clean/disk-dirty must pass,
# staged-dirty/disk-clean must block); the path-list tests alone cannot.
# AC-017 / GI-002 are the last four: a static scan of the shipped sources
# proving no executable line stashes or queries the working tree, so a
# future edit reintroducing the anti-pattern fails this suite.

